SDK descriptors of scripts/setup.sh, one file per SDK, read in the order of
their file names (NN-<key>.conf). setup.sh PARSES them as KEY=value text; it
never sources or runs them. Adding an SDK means adding one descriptor here and
its package directory (with PKGBUILD, configure.sh, selection.sh and,
optionally, download.sh); setup.sh has no per-SDK code: it branches on what a
descriptor holds, never on its key.

Format: blank lines, comment lines (# first), and KEY=value lines; a value is
the rest of the line, taken literally (no quotes, no $, no backtick, no
control character). An unknown key or a duplicate key is an error. Paths of
the installed tree are absolute (setup.sh prefixes them with
MAXINE_SETUP_ROOT); a default_src or post_out beginning with ~/ is under
$HOME; package-relative and root-relative paths have no leading / and no ..
A list is space separated.

Required:
  key           short name: --sdk KEY, --features-KEY, --src-KEY (a-z, 0-9)
  title         the SDK's name in messages
  package       the package directory at the top of the repository; its
                PKGBUILD gives pkgname, pkgver, pkgrel, url (the download
                page) and arch, read as text
  default_src   the default download location (a directory)
  configure     the package's configure.sh (see "The package's scripts")
  byhand_doc    the manual-download instructions (docs/<file>#<anchor>)
  check_doc     the installation check by hand (docs/<file>#<anchor>)
  root          the installed SDK root
  env_file      the installed environment file
  env_prefix    the prefix of its keys (<prefix>_ROOT, _LIBRARY_PATH,
                _FEATURES, and _ARCHS for an SDK with models per
                architecture); <prefix>_SRC is the download location
                variable; lower case, the prefix of selection.sh's functions

How the download is obtained:
  obtain        ngc (the default): from NGC, with the package's download.sh
                and the user's own NGC CLI; a missing download prints the NGC
                steps and offers download.sh.
                browser: one file the user downloads in a browser after
                accepting the licence; a missing download prints the browser
                steps (log in to the NVIDIA Developer Program, open the url,
                Accept & Download download_file, save it in default_src or
                pass --src-KEY) and waits for Enter to re-check or s to skip.
                It never mentions NGC or download.sh.
  download_file the file of a one-file download (required with
                obtain=browser); {version} is the PKGBUILD's pkgver. A
                directory without a file matching it ({version} as *) that
                configure.sh refuses is a missing download. The download
                that configure.sh accepts is selected as the file it reports
                on its "source <path>" line.
  licence       the licence named in the browser steps (default: NVIDIA's
                licence)

configure.sh:
  configure_select  the options `configure --src PATH ... --write` takes
                besides --src and --write: archs (--archs, the detected
                GPU architectures), features (--features all), both (the
                default: "archs features") or none. Only an SDK that takes
                --archs needs a detected GPU.
  checksum_glob the checksum files of a download (each one names the file
                beside it without its last extension), checked after
                configure.sh accepts it; none without it

The installation check (each optional; a column with nothing to check
prints -):
  core_lib      the core library, relative to root, for the ldd check; an
                SDK with one needs a non-empty <prefix>_LIBRARY_PATH (without
                one, an empty or absent library path is "-")
  optional_libs globs, relative to root, of libraries that are ldd'd with
                the env file's library path when they are there
  system_libs   library file names that must be on the system: a path
                check of /usr/lib, /usr/lib64, /lib, /lib64 (under
                MAXINE_SETUP_ROOT when it is set, and only there), else the
                read-only `ldconfig -p`
  check_files   files, relative to root, that must exist
  model_dir     the model directory relative to root (or
                <prefix>_<model_dir_var>); with model_glob
  model_glob    the models below it; {feature} and {arch} (sm_<N>) expand
  model_dir_var the env file key suffix that overrides model_dir

Placeholders (an SDK that is not installable yet):
  status        placeholder: the entry is listed (--help, the SDK choice) as
                "access required", and choosing it (--sdk KEY, or yes to its
                question) only prints how to request access. It is never
                downloaded, configured, built, installed or verified, needs
                no package directory, and --sdk all (or a dry run without
                --sdk) skips it with one line. Only key, title, status and
                the keys below are allowed; any other key is an error.
  request_url   (required) an https page where access is requested
  request_steps (required) the steps, separated by |, printed as a list
  summary       one line shown in --help and before the steps
  licence       the licence the access is under (as above)
  request_note  one more line printed after the request page
                To activate the entry a maintainer adds package and every
                other required key (and the package directory) and removes
                status=placeholder. request_* and summary are errors in an
                active entry.

Optional downloads and features added after the install (obtain=ngc only):
  feature_lib   a feature's library directory below model_dir, beginning
                with {feature} (the feature's own directory, the unit that is
                copied in or reported as not owned by pacman); required
                with post_script
  catalogue     the package's download.sh: its optional downloads are read
                from its array literals (as text) named by
  catalogue_features      the arrays of the names, in order
  catalogue_early_access  the array of the Early Access names
  catalogue_what          the associative array of one-line descriptions
                          (by name, else by the part before the first -)
  catalogue_default       the array of the default selection
  post_script   a script in model_dir that adds features after the install
                (gets NGC_API_KEY in its environment, never on its argv)
  post_args     its arguments; {list} (the effects, comma separated) and
                {out} (post_out) expand
  post_out      the directory it downloads into (required with post_script):
                each run downloads into a new directory below it, and only
                the requested features' directories are copied from there

The package's scripts (the contract setup.sh relies on), with p the
lower-case env_prefix (MAXINE_VFX -> maxine_vfx, NVIDIA_OF -> nvidia_of):
  configure --src PATH        read-only; exit 0 when the download is valid,
                              non-zero with the reason on stderr otherwise
                              (setup.sh prints its first stderr line). setup.sh
                              reads these lines of its output when present:
                              "layout <word>" (tree: an SDK tree, packaged
                              as it is) and "source <absolute path>"
  configure --src PATH [opts] --write   writes the package's selection.conf
  configure --show            prints the selection.conf
  selection.sh                sourced in a subshell; defines
                              p_read_selection <file>, which returns 0 when
                              the file is valid (or absent) and sets
                              p_file_src to its <prefix>_SRC (empty when
                              absent)
  <PREFIX>_SRC                the environment variable configure.sh and the
                              PKGBUILD take the download location from;
                              setup.sh sets it for makepkg to the source it
                              validated (the one a kept selection.conf
                              records, when that differs from --src-KEY or
                              the environment)
